RULING ON THE PRODUCER'S ADDED ONE-WAY RULE ("corrections may only move the ledger toward observed reality -
reconciliation never spends down cycles or layer2_passes"): ACCEPTED. D-22's anti-laundering intent is that no
cheap manoeuvre buys fresh budget (decomposition, rename, runtime hop). D-25 legitimises editing the ledger at
resume, which without a ratchet would be a fourth laundering route - "reconcile" as budget refund. The rule closes
it, and the asymmetry is principled: decrementing tasks_verified is conservative (claims less delivered work),
decrementing cycles is not (claims less spend). Residual wording defect (low): in a genuine OVER-count the two
clauses conflict - "move toward observed reality" would decrement while "never spends down cycles" forbids it.
The safe direction wins by default (spurious exhaustion -> human fork), but precedence should be stated.

